{"slug":"identity","number":"3","title":"Identity and references","file":"spec/core/03-identity.md","sections":[{"id":"3.1","number":"3.1","title":"Element IDs"},{"id":"3.2","number":"3.2","title":"References"},{"id":"3.3","number":"3.3","title":"Level consistency"}],"blocks":[{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"3.1","number":"3.1","c":["Element IDs"]},{"t":"p","c":["An element's ID is its member name in its collection. IDs are opaque: nothing may be inferred from an ID's spelling. The reference implementation mints short, kind-prefixed IDs — ",{"t":"code","v":"W12"}," for a wall, ",{"t":"code","v":"J4"}," for a junction, ",{"t":"code","v":"R5"}," for a room — because they are easy to read aloud and to type; UUIDs are equally conformant."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-3.1.1","level":"MUST","c":["An element ID MUST match the pattern ",{"t":"code","v":"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$"},"."]}]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-3.1.2","level":"MUST","c":["An element ID MUST be unique across all of a document's collections, not only within its own."]}," A reference can therefore never be ambiguous, and a diagnostic can name an element by its ID alone."]},{"t":"p","c":["Program items (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/program#11.1","c":["11.1"]},") and extension elements (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/extensions#12.5","c":["12.5"]},") share this space of IDs: the program's ",{"t":"code","v":"items"}," and every collection an extension adds count as collections for ",{"t":"a","href":"#FS-CORE-3.1.2","c":["3.1.2"]},"."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-3.1.3","level":"MUST","c":["A program item's ID and an extension element's ID MUST match the pattern of ",{"t":"a","href":"#FS-CORE-3.1.1","c":["3.1.1"]},", and MUST be unique among all the IDs of the document, as element IDs are."]}]},{"t":"callout","kind":"note","title":["IDs across versions"],"c":[{"t":"p","c":["An ID identifies one element for as long as it exists: an edit changes an element's members, never its ID, and a deleted element's ID is not reused. That is a property of edits, so Floorspec Ops states it normatively; a single document cannot show it."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"3.2","number":"3.2","c":["References"]},{"t":"p","c":["A ",{"t":"strong","c":["reference"]}," is a member whose value is the ID of another element. Every reference names the collection — and, for types, the kind — of the element it must resolve to. For this section the program's ",{"t":"code","v":"items"}," is a collection, and a program item or an extension element that holds a reference is its referring element:"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null],"head":[["Element"],["Member"],["Resolves to"]],"rows":[[["Level"],[{"t":"code","v":"building"}],["a building"]],[["Junction, Wall, Separator, Room, Slab"],[{"t":"code","v":"level"}],["a level"]],[["Wall, Separator"],[{"t":"code","v":"start"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"end"}],["a junction"]],[["Wall"],[{"t":"code","v":"type"}],["a type of kind ",{"t":"code","v":"wallType"}]],[["Wall"],[{"t":"code","v":"base.level"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"top.level"}],["a level"]],[["Junction"],[{"t":"code","v":"join.through[]"}],["a wall (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/walls#5.8","c":["5.8"]},")"]],[["Opening"],[{"t":"code","v":"wall"}],["a wall"]],[["Opening"],[{"t":"code","v":"fill"}],["a type of kind ",{"t":"code","v":"doorType"}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"windowType"}]],[["Layer (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/types#8.3","c":["8.3"]},")"],[{"t":"code","v":"material"}],["a material"]],[["Room"],[{"t":"code","v":"wallFinish"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"floorFinish"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"ceilingFinish"}],["a material"]],[["Slab"],[{"t":"code","v":"material"}],["a material"]],[["Material"],[{"t":"code","v":"texture.asset"}],["an asset"]],[["Material"],[{"t":"code","v":"texture.normal"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"texture.metallicRoughness"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"texture.occlusion"}],["an asset (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/materials#18.2","c":["18.2"]},")"]],[["Wall"],[{"t":"code","v":"finishes.left.material"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"finishes.right.material"},", and the ",{"t":"code","v":"material"}," of each of their ",{"t":"code","v":"regions"}],["a material (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/materials#18.5","c":["18.5"]},")"]],[["Room"],[{"t":"code","v":"brief"}],["a program item (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/program#11.3","c":["11.3"]},")"]],[["Program item"],[{"t":"code","v":"level"}],["a level"]],[["Adjacency (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/program#11.2","c":["11.2"]},")"],[{"t":"code","v":"a"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"b"}],["a program item"]],[["Extension element (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/extensions#12.5","c":["12.5"]},")"],[{"t":"code","v":"host.wall"}],["a wall (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/hosting#13.3","c":["13.3"]},")"]],[["Extension element"],[{"t":"code","v":"host.room"}],["a room"]],[["Extension element"],[{"t":"code","v":"host.level"}],["a level"]],[["Extension element"],[{"t":"code","v":"fallback.level"}],["a level (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/extensions#12.6","c":["12.6"]},")"]],[["Extension element"],[{"t":"code","v":"fallback.asset"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"fallback.symbol"}],["an asset"]],[["Stair"],[{"t":"code","v":"level"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"to"}],["a level (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/stairs#17.1","c":["17.1"]},")"]],[["Option"],[{"t":"code","v":"set"}],["an option set (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/options#19.1","c":["19.1"]},")"]],[["Option set"],[{"t":"code","v":"primary"}],["an option (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/options#19.1","c":["19.1"]},")"]],[["Junction, Wall, Separator, Opening, Room, Slab, Roof, Stair, Extension element"],[{"t":"code","v":"option"}],["an option (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/options#19.2","c":["19.2"]},")"]]]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-3.2.3","level":"MUST","c":["A reference MUST be a string that matches the ID pattern of ",{"t":"a","href":"#3.1","c":["3.1"]},"."]}]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-3.2.1","level":"MUST","c":["Every reference MUST resolve to an element of the collection that its member names in this table."]}]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-3.2.2","level":"MUST","c":["Every reference to a type MUST resolve to a type of the kind its member names in this table."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"3.3","number":"3.3","c":["Level consistency"]},{"t":"p","c":["Elements that meet on a plan meet on one level."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-3.3.1","level":"MUST","c":["A wall's or separator's ",{"t":"code","v":"start"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"end"}," junctions MUST be on the wall's or separator's own level."]}]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-3.3.2","level":"MUST","c":["A level named by a wall's ",{"t":"code","v":"base.level"}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"top.level"}," MUST be in the same building as the wall's own level."]}]}]}
